<title>USA: Burr-Brown says to cut workforce by 4 pct.</title>
<headline>Burr-Brown says to cut workforce by 4 pct.</headline>
<dateline>TUCSON, Ariz 1996-09-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Burr-Brown Corp said on Thursday it has reduced its workforce by 60 people, or about four percent of its total employees.</p>
<p>The company cited the overall softness of demand for the semiconducter industry and said that about 80 percent of the reductions occurred in the manufacturing and operations area.  </p>
<p>The company added that it expects third quarter results to be at or near market consensus.</p>
<p>According to First Call mean consensus estimates, analysts' projections for the current third quarter are for earnings per share of $0.33.</p>
</text>
